From: mayipashu <mayipashu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: npu: wait for the firmware bring-up signature
 before querying its version

The MT7916 NPU firmware (en7581_MT7916_npu_rv32.bin) needs roughly a second
after the BOOT_TRIGGER pulse before its cores and QDMA data path are up. It
publishes 0xcccccccc in the last MIB register only once that finished.

The driver queried WLAN_FUNC_GET_WAIT_NPU_VERSION 100 ms after the pulse and
gave up, so probe logged "NPU firmware did not answer the version query" and
every later mailbox command failed, even though the message layout, the
mailbox registers and the doorbell order are shared with the firmware.

Measured on H3C HM2004-DU by booting the very same image from the shell with
the driver's own sequence (MIB10/BOOT_BASE/BOOT_CONFIG=0xff, TRIGGER 0->1):
the cores start, MIB31 reads 0xcccccccc after ~1 s, and a hand-built
version query then returns DONE with status 0. Booting the same image
without MIB10 and BOOT_BASE (a plain trigger pulse) leaves every core at
PC 0, which is why the legacy-ABI path never worked either.

Poll MIB31 for the signature and retry the version query a few times, so
probe only continues once the firmware actually answers.

Signed-off-by: mayipashu <mayipashu@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
@@ -53,6 +53,10 @@
 #define REG_CR_MBQ8_CTRL(_n)		(NPU_MBOX_BASE_ADDR + 0x0b0 + ((_n) << 2))
 #define REG_CR_NPU_MIB(_n)		(NPU_MBOX_BASE_ADDR + 0x140 + ((_n) << 2))
 
+/* last MIB register: the firmware stores its bring-up signature here */
+#define NPU_BOOT_SIGNATURE_REG		REG_CR_NPU_MIB(31)
+#define NPU_BOOT_SIGNATURE_COMPLETE	0xcccccccc
+
 #define NPU_WLAN_BASE_ADDR		0x30d000
 
 #define REG_IRQ_STATUS			(NPU_WLAN_BASE_ADDR + 0x030)
@@ -865,12 +869,35 @@
 	/* enable NPU cores */
 	regmap_write(npu->regmap, REG_CR_BOOT_CONFIG, 0xff);
 	regmap_write(npu->regmap, REG_CR_BOOT_TRIGGER, 0x1);
-	msleep(100);
 
-	if (!airoha_npu_wlan_msg_get(npu, 0, WLAN_FUNC_GET_WAIT_NPU_VERSION,
-				     &val, sizeof(val), GFP_KERNEL))
-		dev_info(dev, "NPU fw version: %0d.%d\n",
-			 (val >> 16) & 0xffff, val & 0xffff);
+	/*
+	 * The MT7916 NPU firmware needs about a second to bring its cores and
+	 * the QDMA data path up, and only then publishes
+	 * NPU_BOOT_SIGNATURE_COMPLETE in the last MIB register. Querying the
+	 * version before that signature is visible times out even though both
+	 * sides agree on the message layout (verified on H3C HM2004-DU with the
+	 * en7581_MT7916 image: the very same query returns status 0 as soon as
+	 * the firmware is really running).
+	 */
+	err = regmap_read_poll_timeout(npu->regmap, NPU_BOOT_SIGNATURE_REG,
+				       val, val == NPU_BOOT_SIGNATURE_COMPLETE,
+				       2000, 5 * USEC_PER_SEC);
+	if (err)
+		dev_warn(dev, "firmware bring-up incomplete, MIB31=%#x\n", val);
+
+	/* the first query can still race the firmware's mailbox setup */
+	for (i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
+		if (!airoha_npu_wlan_msg_get(npu, 0,
+					     WLAN_FUNC_GET_WAIT_NPU_VERSION,
+					     &val, sizeof(val), GFP_KERNEL)) {
+			dev_info(dev, "NPU fw version: %0d.%d\n",
+				 (val >> 16) & 0xffff, val & 0xffff);
+			break;
+		}
+		msleep(20);
+	}
+	if (i == 5)
+		dev_warn(dev, "NPU firmware did not answer the version query\n");
 
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, npu);
 
